{
 "slug": "budapest",
 "lines": [
  {
   "o": 0.424,
   "text": "Before 1873, you could stare at Pest from Buda... and still be stuck for days. So how did two cities become Budapest?",
   "chunks": [
    "BEFORE *1873,*",
    "YOU COULD STARE AT|*PEST* FROM *BUDA...*",
    "AND STILL BE STUCK|FOR *DAYS.*",
    "SO HOW DID|*TWO CITIES*",
    "BECOME *BUDAPEST?*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 8.866,
   "text": "On this side: Buda. Hills, a royal castle.",
   "chunks": [
    "ON THIS SIDE: *BUDA.*",
    "HILLS, A|*ROYAL CASTLE.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 12.116,
   "text": "On that side: Pest. Flat, busy, full of merchants.",
   "chunks": [
    "ON THAT SIDE: *PEST.*",
    "FLAT, BUSY, FULL|OF *MERCHANTS.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 16.053,
   "text": "We have a castle.",
   "chunks": [
    "WE HAVE A *CASTLE.*"
   ],
   "speaker": "buda"
  },
  {
   "o": 17.493,
   "text": "We have customers.",
   "chunks": [
    "WE HAVE *CUSTOMERS.*"
   ],
   "speaker": "pest"
  },
  {
   "o": 19.25,
   "text": "But between them ran the Danube... with no permanent bridge.",
   "chunks": [
    "BUT BETWEEN THEM|RAN THE *DANUBE...*",
    "WITH *NO*|PERMANENT *BRIDGE.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 23.083,
   "text": "So how do you glue two cities together?",
   "chunks": [
    "SO HOW DO YOU *GLUE*|TWO CITIES TOGETHER?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 25.537,
   "text": "Not easily. When the river froze, even the bridge of boats was useless. The nearest real bridge? Vienna. 250 kilometres away.",
   "chunks": [
    "NOT EASILY.",
    "WHEN THE RIVER *FROZE,*",
    "EVEN THE BRIDGE|OF *BOATS*",
    "WAS *USELESS.*",
    "THE NEAREST|REAL BRIDGE?",
    "*VIENNA.*",
    "*250 KILOMETRES* AWAY."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 34.934,
   "text": "The story goes... in 1820, Count Széchenyi reached this river, on his way to his father's funeral.",
   "chunks": [
    "THE STORY GOES...",
    "IN *1820,* COUNT|*SZÉCHENYI*",
    "REACHED THIS RIVER,",
    "ON HIS WAY TO HIS|FATHER'S *FUNERAL.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 41.274,
   "text": "The ice wouldn't let him cross. He waited about a week... and missed it.",
   "chunks": [
    "THE *ICE* WOULDN'T|LET HIM CROSS.",
    "HE WAITED ABOUT|A *WEEK...*",
    "AND *MISSED IT.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 45.657,
   "text": "So he pushed for a permanent bridge.",
   "chunks": [
    "SO HE PUSHED FOR A|*PERMANENT BRIDGE.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 47.829,
   "text": "Two British engineers built it. Both named Clark. Not related.",
   "chunks": [
    "TWO BRITISH|ENGINEERS BUILT IT.",
    "BOTH NAMED *CLARK.*",
    "*NOT RELATED.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 51.959,
   "text": "In 1849, the Chain Bridge opened. And on it, even nobles had to pay the toll.",
   "chunks": [
    "IN *1849,* THE|*CHAIN BRIDGE* OPENED.",
    "AND ON IT, EVEN|*NOBLES*",
    "HAD TO PAY|THE *TOLL.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 57.51,
   "text": "I have to pay? To walk?",
   "chunks": [
    "I HAVE TO *PAY?*|TO *WALK?*"
   ],
   "speaker": "noble"
  },
  {
   "o": 59.647,
   "text": "The cities grew together... and in 1873, they merged. Buda, plus Pest... Budapest.",
   "chunks": [
    "THE CITIES GREW|TOGETHER...",
    "AND IN *1873,*|THEY *MERGED.*",
    "*BUDA,* PLUS *PEST...*",
    "*BUDAPEST.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 66.239,
   "text": "Except... it was never just two cities.",
   "chunks": [
    "EXCEPT...",
    "IT WAS NEVER JUST|*TWO* CITIES."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 69.405,
   "text": "A third town joined that day: Óbuda. Literally, Old Buda.",
   "chunks": [
    "A *THIRD TOWN*|JOINED THAT DAY:",
    "*ÓBUDA.*",
    "LITERALLY, *OLD BUDA.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 74.115,
   "text": "And nobody puts me in the name.",
   "chunks": [
    "AND *NOBODY* PUTS|ME IN THE *NAME.*"
   ],
   "speaker": "obuda"
  },
  {
   "o": 76.292,
   "text": "This is BHUGOL. Follow for more Geography Fun Facts.",
   "chunks": [
    "THIS IS *BHUGOL.*",
    "FOLLOW FOR MORE|GEOGRAPHY FUN FACTS."
   ]
  }
 ],
